#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
ThinkPad fan control daemon, v2.

Samples the thermal sensors once per second, filters them with two EMAs
(a fast one for the rising path, a slow one for the falling path), walks a
fan curve whose steps carry their own release temperatures, and drives
/proc/acpi/ibm/fan.  It publishes its decision state for the GUI
(state.json / history.json), answers a small control socket (manual holds),
plays the critical alert as the desktop user without sudo, and keeps the
EC watchdog fed so a dead daemon hands the fan back to the firmware.

docs/CONTRACT.md is the binding specification; "§n" in comments refers to
its sections.  Where the contract left room, the safer behaviour for the
hardware was chosen and the reason is written next to the code.

Self-contained on purpose: this runs as root, so it imports nothing from a
user-writable directory (Python 3.12 stdlib only).

Layout:
  environment        paths, level table, GUI identity from daemon.env
  config             DEFAULTS, sanitize(), v1 migration, --save-config
  logging            dense log lines, WARN/ERROR rate limiting
  hardware           hwmon by name, /proc/acpi/ibm/fan, AC, sd_notify, alerts
  Controller         the decision logic; drives an injected HAL and clock
  live daemon        selectors loop, control socket, state/history files,
                     startup wait, self-test
  simulation         fake clock/HAL, v1 rules, thermal model, --simulate
  trace generator    --gen-trace scenarios
  CLI
"""

